     2,
     "On 11/28/2012 08:30 PM, Robert wrote:\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Dear Yves,\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; the observation regarding the change score models, have been based on\r<br>&gt; another data set of mine. in order to provide anyone with the\r<br>&gt; opportunity to easily replicate my findings, i wrote the commented R\r<br>&gt; code you referred to. however, as soon as i posted it, i notice some\r<br>&gt; serious flaws and tried to delete it, which was obviously not as\r<br>&gt; successful as expected.. anyway\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; please find the revision below. furthermore i copy-pasted the results\r<br>&gt; from the same code having been executed with lavaan versions 0.5.10. and\r<br>&gt; 0.4.14:\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "Confirmed. This is a result of a bug in 0.5-10 (which was reported in \r<br>the context of (composite latent variables), where zero-variances are \r<br>set to 1, affecting all post-fitting operations, including predict().\r<br>\r<br>To be clear, this bug will only manifest itself if a variance (here, the \r<br>residual variance for y) needs to be set to zero. It does not affect \r<br>estimation, nor the summary results.\r<br>\r<br>The good news is: this bug was already fixed in the dev version. To \r<br>install the dev version, type this in R:\r<br>\r<br>install.packages(&quot;pbivnorm&quot;)\r<br>install.packages(&quot;lavaan&quot;, repos=&quot;http:/<a href=\"http://www.da.ugent.be\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.da.ugent.be&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792433385586000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2LXfSGzfBpBtcKc2tNMyqb\">www.da.ugent.be</a>&quot;, type=&quot;source&quot;)\r<br>\r<br>Yves.\r<br>\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
